(a) Existing driveways. All those persons who as of March 17, 2009 had driveways crossing the railroad recreation trail shall continue to be entitled to cross the railroad recreation trail for the sole purpose of access[ing] their respective property along the entire length of the railroad recreation trail.
(b) New driveways or crossings. Driveways or crossings of the railroad recreation trails not existing on March 17, 2009 shall not be permitted or authorized to be constructed or cross the railroad recreation trail except with and under the following limited conditions:
(1) All requests for new driveways and crossings must be submitted in writing to and approved by the Board of Commissioners of Harris County based on all of the terms and conditions which follow hereafter;
(2) A survey with proposed grade, drainage, utilities and public rights-of-way shall be prepared at the cost of the applicant and submitted along with a written request for a new driveway or crossing;
(3) No new driveways or crossings shall be authorized or approved by the Board of Commissioners of Harris County if the property for which a driveway or crossing is sought fronts on or has access to a public road or a private road or access easement. New driveways or crossings may be permitted or approved only if the property to be accessed by the new driveway or crossing is otherwise landlocked;
(4) To maintain the integrity of the non-motorized walkway for pedestrian and bicycle use, all proposed new driveways or crossings should not cause or result in any increase or decrease in the elevation of the existing surface of the former railroad bed if at all possible. However, it is recognized that new driveways or crossings may require slight elevation changes to allow vehicular access. In such cases, the required survey shall delineate the existing grade and the proposed grade, along with all other information required for the survey as required by this section. The proposed grade change shall be reviewed by the county's engineer, and the county's engineer shall provide a recommendation on whether the proposed grade change is necessary for vehicular access over the proposed driveway or crossing and whether the proposed grade change is suitable for pedestrian and bicycle use with the least impact on the existing grade in order to maintain the necessary integrity of the non-motorized walkway;
(5) Any proposed new driveways or crossings shall not negatively impact the drainage path within the railroad right-of-way or roadway ditches and drainage. Driveways or road culverts and ditch grading may be required for any proposed new driveways or crossings;
(6) Any proposed new driveways or crossings to a federal, state or county road or highway shall have the approval of the respective road or highway entity as for sight distance or other requirements of the entity owning or controlling the public right-of-way;
(7) Multiple side-by-side new driveways or crossings shall not be permitted; new driveways or crossings from a land area must be limited to one;
(8) All costs for design, construction, and maintenance of driveways or crossings applications and approvals under section 3.5-54(b) shall be at the expense of the person or entity seeking the driveway or crossing and any subsequent owners thereof; and
(9) If a new driveway or crossing is permitted and approved by the Board of Commissioners of Harris County, the applicant shall be granted only a license to use such crossing of the railbed. The license is permissive in use and shall be a mere accommodation and shall be revocable at any time by the Board of Commissioners of Harris County. The license shall not grant and the applicant shall not acquire any ownership rights to the railbed property, whether in fee simple, by prescription or by adverse possession.
(Ord. No. 01-09, § 14, 3-17-2009; Ord. No. 05-19, § 2, 11-5-2019; Ord. No. 02-22, §§ 1, 2, 6-21-2022)

